{"title":"1","text":"<div class=\"mw-content-ltr mw-parser-output\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><p>One, or unity, is the smallest positive integer. It is commonly shown using the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Arabic_numeral&amp;action=edit&amp;redlink=1\" class=\"new\" title=\"Arabic numeral (page does not exist)\">Arabic numeral</a> 1, and sometimes is denoted by the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roman_numeral\" title=\"Roman numeral\">Roman numeral</a> I. 1 is neither <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Prime\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Prime\">prime</a> or <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Composite\" class=\"mw-redirect\" title=\"Composite\">composite</a>.\n</p>\n<div id=\"toc\" class=\"toc\" role=\"navigation\" aria-labelledby=\"mw-toc-heading\"><input type=\"checkbox\" role=\"button\" id=\"toctogglecheckbox\" class=\"toctogglecheckbox\" style=\"display:none\" /><div class=\"toctitle\" lang=\"en\" dir=\"ltr\"><h2 id=\"mw-toc-heading\">Contents</h2><span class=\"toctogglespan\"><label class=\"toctogglelabel\" for=\"toctogglecheckbox\"></label></span></div>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-1\"><a href=\"#Operations\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Operations</span></a>\n<ul>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-2\"><a href=\"#Addition\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.1</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Addition</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-3\"><a href=\"#Subtraction\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Subtraction</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-4\"><a href=\"#Multiplication\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.3</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Multiplication</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-5\"><a href=\"#Division\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.4</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Division</span></a></li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-2 tocsection-6\"><a href=\"#Exponents\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">1.5</span> <span class=\"toctext\">Exponents</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</li>\n<li class=\"toclevel-1 tocsection-7\"><a href=\"#See_Also\"><span class=\"tocnumber\">2</span> <span class=\"toctext\">See Also</span></a></li>\n</ul>\n</div>\n\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Operations\">Operations</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=1\" title=\"Edit section: Operations\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Addition\">Addition</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=2\" title=\"Edit section: Addition\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Addition by one is also known as the <a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Successor_function\" title=\"Successor function\">Successor function</a>. When you add one to a number, it increases by 1. For example, \\(5+1=6\\).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Subtraction\">Subtraction</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=3\" title=\"Edit section: Subtraction\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>When a number is subtracted by one, the number is decreased by one. For example, \\(3-1=2\\).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Multiplication\">Multiplication</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=4\" title=\"Edit section: Multiplication\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Any number multiplied by 1 equals the number. For example, \\(4 \\cdot 1 = 4 \\), and \\(9 \\cdot 1 = 9 \\). This is why 1 is known as the multiplicative identity.\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Division\">Division</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=5\" title=\"Edit section: Division\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Any number divided by one is that same number. For example, \\( \\frac{6}{1} = 6 \\), and \\( \\frac{7}{1} = 7 \\).\n</p>\n<h3><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"Exponents\">Exponents</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=6\" title=\"Edit section: Exponents\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h3>\n<p>Any number to the power of 1 is that number. This is because a number to the power of 1 means that there is a product with only one number, which in this case is the number to the power of 1.\n</p>\n<h2><span class=\"mw-headline\" id=\"See_Also\">See Also</span><span class=\"mw-editsection\"><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">[</span><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit&amp;section=7\" title=\"Edit section: See Also\">edit</a><span class=\"mw-editsection-bracket\">]</span></span></h2>\n<ul><li><a href=\"/wiki/index.php?title=Roots_of_unity\" title=\"Roots of unity\">Roots of unity</a></li></ul>\n<p><i>This article is a stub.  Help us out by <span class=\"plainlinks\"><a rel=\"nofollow\" class=\"external text\" href=\"https://artofproblemsolving.com/wiki/index.php?title=1&amp;action=edit\">expanding it</a></span>.</i>\n</p>\n<!-- \nNewPP limit report\nCached time: 20261017091116\nCache expiry: 86400\nReduced expiry: false\nComplications: [show‐toc]\nCPU time usage: 0.014 seconds\nReal time usage: 0.031 seconds\nPreprocessor visited node count: 32/1000000\nPost‐expand include size: 244/2097152 bytes\nTemplate argument size: 0/2097152 bytes\nHighest expansion depth: 4/100\nExpensive parser function count: 0/100\nUnstrip recursion depth: 0/20\nUnstrip post‐expand size: 0/5000000 bytes\n-->\n<!--\nTransclusion expansion time report (%,ms,calls,template)\n100.00%    5.370      1 Template:Stub\n100.00%    5.370      1 -total\n-->\n\n<!-- Saved in parser cache with key wiki-wiki_:pcache:16463:|#|:idhash:canonical and timestamp 20261017091116 and revision id 273796. Rendering was triggered because: page-view\n -->\n</div>"}